From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Moritz=20Mei=C3=9Felbach?= <moritz@glassine.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:38:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] freedreno/a5xx: barrier() compute with >1 wave per
 workgroup (A509 hangs)

Two fixes, found on the Adreno 509 (Boox Note Air 1, Mesa 25.1.9; ported to 26.1.6):

1. fd5_compute.c wrote 0x1 to HLSQ_CS_CNTL_1. Like a6xx's LINEARLOCALIDREGID,
   it names a register (0x1 = r0.y), which ir3 never asks for. With it, compute
   shaders with barrier() and more than one wave per workgroup hang the GPU
   (hang detect, status E40801C1) or compute garbage, e.g. a 12.8 KB shared
   array at 128 invocations. regid(63, 0) (none) fixes them; plain shaders
   without barriers saw no difference in their invocation ids
   (a probe over 5 workgroup shapes).

2. ir3_ra.c: calc_limit_pressure_for_cs_with_barrier only capped the register
   pressure with merged registers (a6xx+); a4xx/a5xx have a separate half
   file, and RA always sized it RA_HALF_SIZE. A shader with 48 half vec4 at
   128 invocations could not keep all its waves resident and hung at the
   barrier. Cap full and half per wave there and bound the half file by the
   cap.

With both, a 128-invocation layered error-diffusion shader with 8 barriers
is byte-exact and fault-free; stock faults on every dispatch. 256 invocations
still fault (a third limit, open).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (unreviewed; tested only on the A509)
---
 src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c                    | 24 ++++++++++++-------
 .../drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_compute.c      |  7 +++++-
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c
index 1f951591808..8e7e37d334c 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c
@@ -2738,14 +2738,20 @@ calc_limit_pressure_for_cs_with_barrier(struct ir3_shader_variant *v,
 
    uint32_t half_regs_per_thread = vec4_regs_per_thread * 4 * 2;
 
-   if (limit_pressure->full > half_regs_per_thread) {
-      if (v->mergedregs) {
+   if (v->mergedregs) {
+      if (limit_pressure->full > half_regs_per_thread)
          limit_pressure->full = half_regs_per_thread;
-      } else {
-         /* TODO: Handle !mergedregs case, probably we would have to do this
-          * after the first register pressure pass.
-          */
-      }
+   } else {
+      /* a4xx/a5xx: the full and the half register files are separate, each
+       * of reg_size_vec4 parts; both must leave room for every wave of the
+       * workgroup, or the waves that don't fit never reach the barrier and
+       * the GPU hangs (A509: 48 half vec4 at 128 invocations). Full pressure
+       * counts in half-register units, half pressure in half registers.
+       */
+      if (limit_pressure->full > half_regs_per_thread)
+         limit_pressure->full = half_regs_per_thread;
+      if (limit_pressure->half > vec4_regs_per_thread * 4)
+         limit_pressure->half = vec4_regs_per_thread * 4;
    }
 }
 
@@ -2876,8 +2882,10 @@ ir3_ra(struct ir3_shader_variant *v)
    assert(ctx->full.size <= RA_FULL_SIZE);
    d("full size: %u", ctx->full.size);
 
+   /* (separate half file: the barrier cap must bound the file, not only the
+    * pressure, or the allocator still spreads into the top half registers) */
    if (!v->mergedregs)
-      ctx->half.size = RA_HALF_SIZE;
+      ctx->half.size = MIN2(RA_HALF_SIZE, limit_pressure.half);
 
    ctx->shared.size = RA_SHARED_SIZE;
 
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_compute.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_compute.c
index 64f6199d8dc..f9209b16c9e 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_compute.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a5xx/fd5_compute.c
@@ -80,7 +80,12 @@ cs_program_emit(struct fd_context *ctx, struct fd_ringbuffer *ring, struct ir3_s
                      A5XX_HLSQ_CS_CNTL_0_UNK0(regid(63, 0)) |
                      A5XX_HLSQ_CS_CNTL_0_UNK1(regid(63, 0)) |
                      A5XX_HLSQ_CS_CNTL_0_LOCALIDREGID(local_invocation_id));
-   OUT_RING(ring, 0x1); /* HLSQ_CS_CNTL_1 */
+   /* HLSQ_CS_CNTL_1 holds the linear local id register, as on a6xx
+    * (LINEARLOCALIDREGID): ir3 never asks for it, so r63.x = none. The old
+    * 0x1 (r0.y) made compute shaders with barrier() and more than one wave
+    * per workgroup hang the A509 (hang detect) or compute garbage.
+    */
+   OUT_RING(ring, regid(63, 0)); /* HLSQ_CS_CNTL_1 */
 
    if (instrlen > 0)
       fd5_emit_shader(ring, v);
